> I was wondering if there are any kind Nethackers who wouldn't mind
> offering me some advice, but not really spoilers.

There are many people here who I'm sure will offer help.  I'll give
some pointers but the difference between "spoilers" and "advice" can be
subjective but I'll do my best ...

Here are a few off the top of my head:
Waste not, want not;
haste makes waste.

Stash up all of your loot and over the course of 100k turns or so
you'll have more than enough.  With sufficient stats and gear,
ascending will be easier than the early game, ermm, well maybe, it
_could_ be.

> Anyhow, a quick game locally one night before bed spiraled into a massive
> epic game after I found a Wand of Wishing on level:4 :)

Nice!  That's the same RNG that gives gnomes wands of death so take
what you get!

> In my current game here are my details:
>
> IcyValk77 the Warrior   St:18/** Dx:20 Co:18 In:21 Wi:21 Ch:14 Neutral
> Dlvl:15 $:0  HP:174(174) Pw:84(84) AC:-18 Xp:16/359536 T:98376
> Blind

Although it's nice to run around with a towel around one's head it can
be dangerous and you'll feel silly if you die because of it.  For one
thing you won't see green slimes or ochre jellies, etc. if you are
using telepathy.

>  Amulets
>  t - an uncursed amulet of life saving

You should wear this.

>  Weapons
>  I - the blessed rustproof +3 Fire Brand (weapon in hand)

Review your list of possible artifact weapons and consider the likely
entities that would be living in the smoky, sulphury place that is
Gehennom.  Perhaps there is a more appropriate weapon for those foes?
Also, you've probably noticed that Fire Brand burns monsters and
sometimes their belongings; many weapons affect monster's inventories
so give some thought to the tradeoffs of the special abilities of
artifact weapons.

> I have a stash on Dlvl:20 filled with Dragonbane, Frostbrand, about 80k in
> gold and tons of other kit.

Since you have so much gold perhaps you should make use of the oracle's
services?  Like a previous poster said, it's there to help.   although
much of the minor consultations are a bit hard to interpret.  Still,
you might as well use the gold.  Unless you can think of somewhere else
to spend it (hint) ...

> All altars that I've found so far I have converted to Odin. Well, except
> those with a priest.  Should I try to convert these or is it bad?  I think
> I can take the priest but when I've killed a priest of a different
> alignment in the past, I'm sure bad things have happened.

Since you asked specifically, angering priests, unless you want their
robes and gear, does not avail you of much except for the opportunity
to use their altar.  Also, instead of killing everything that you see,
why not try #chatting sometimes?

It's refreshing to hear about the travails of an unspoiled player.
Best of luck and keep on having fun hacking!



